{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/449777-mystery-the-mystery-of-vitalic-philosophy","id":449777,"title":"[Mystery] The Mystery of Vitalic Philosophy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-19T14:43:53-07:00","id":449777,"title":"[Mystery] The Mystery of Vitalic Philosophy","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Mystery of Vitalic Philosophy</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">This is not a single Mystery; instead, there is a version for each Discipline, Coil, and Blood Sorcery. You cannot have more dots in this Coil than you have in the corresponding &quot;Discipline&quot;; in addition, the limitation on &quot;instances&quot; of this Mystery's effects applies to all versions of this Mystery. The knowledge of this Mystery (and it's corresponding Coil) are held as strictly heretical, given the ease that a Master has at ignoring any limitations regarding not teaching Coils to an outsider. No one has been able to develop a version of this Coil tied to another version of this Coil, but this does not mean that there haven't been attempts.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Coil of Vitalic Philosophy (or the Coil of [Discipline] Philosophy)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Strengthened Vitae (\u2022)</b>: The Dragon's Vitae seethes and riots within their veins, bringing about a targeted personal evolution. Upon waking from Daysleep, the Dragon may apply an instance of this Coil to themselves, the benefits of which last until the next dawn. They may have up to two instances of this Coil active at once, with each instance past the first costing one Vitae to apply. At this point, they may only apply the following benefits; they do stack with each-other.</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2022 They are considered to have an additional dot of the Discipline for the sole purpose of determining the benefits of the active effects of the Discipline.<br /> \u2022 They receive a +1 bonus to the activation roll for the Discipline; for every two instances of this benefit, they receive an additional +1 bonus to the activation roll.</span></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Manipulation of Vital Fluids (\u2022\u2022):</b> The seething vitae brings its own benefits now; for one, the number of instances of this Coil that may be active at once increases by one (to a maximum of five). Similarly, the Dragon may &quot;gift&quot; an instance of this Coil to a Ghoul or Kindred by feeding them one Vitae; instead of adding their Vitae to their pool, the recipient gains a benefit chosen by the Dragon. They also expand what &quot;benefits&quot; they may grant to include the following:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2022 As long as they remain within the Dragon's field of vision, the Dragon may veto any active use of that Discipline as a Reflexive action; if their Blood Potency is higher than the Dragon's, this veto costs the Dragon one Willpower.<br /> \u2022 The Dragon is entirely immune to their use of the Discipline; this does not protect them from the consequences of the Discipline's use, only the direct effects of the Discipline.</span></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Controlling the Scarlet Flow (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> The might of the Dragon's vital control is evident; the number of instances of this Coil that may be active at once increases by one (to a maximum of five). Additionally, any attempt to activate a Discipline by a character affected by an instance of this Coil receives the 9-again quality. The following &quot;benefits&quot; become available to the Dragon:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2022 The cost to activate the Discipline for the first time each Scene is reduced by one Vitae.<br /> \u2022 They lose a dot of that Discipline for the duration.</span></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Creating Blood-Borne Power (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><b>:</b> The Dragon has moved beyond simply controlling blood-borne powers to creating them wholesale; this is what takes this Coil from an idle curiosity to a dire heresy that is to be rooted out with fire. The number of instances of this Coil that may be active at once increases by one (to a maximum of five), and any Discipline by a character affected by an instance of this Coil achieves an Exceptional Success with three successes rather than three. In addition, the following options becomes available as an instance of this Coil:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2022 They gain a dot of the Discipline (to a maximum of five).<br /> \u2022 They gain up to 3xp worth of Devotions for the Discipline. They must qualify for the Devotions.</span></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Muse of Cruor and Gore (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> This Coil is rarely, if ever finished; most adherents are staked to face the morning light before they ever reach this point. Still, the few that have reached this point have become veritable gods of blood, twisting and coiling Vitae within the veins of others. The Dragon may now apply an instance of this Coil to any Ghoul or Kindred that makes eye-contact with them by spending one Vitae as a reflexive action, may apply an instance of this Coil to themselves at any time by spending one Vitae as an Instant action, and may reflexively the benefits of - or even entirely remove - an instance of the Coil applied to any character they can see or touch by spending one Willpower as a reflexive action.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> So, yes, I'm still trying to come up with Scales for this one.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? I'd love to hear them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:55:37-07:00","id":450664,"title":"","content":"Seems interesting. I might not be the most mechanically inclined, but wouldn't having to buy it at full cost for each whatever be rather expensive? Also, I hate to sound rude or anything, but wouldn't allowing it to &quot;teach&quot; Coils kind of go against the whole thing the Mysteries represent? Otherwise, pretty awesome idea! As for Scales, maybe something that can temporarily make a mortal into a Ghoul or Revenant, call it &quot;Taste of Power&quot;, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:36:49-07:00","id":450705,"title":"","content":"You're probably right about it being a bit over-costly; I kinda wrote this up after being awake for too long.<br /> <br /> As for Teaching Coils, that bit was... ill advised on my part; most of the effects of the Coil don't work well with how Coils are structured.<br /> <br /> That Scale sounds good!<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to post a revised version at some point today that works more like a Coil (this used to be five Devotions, and it shows.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:11:56-07:00","id":450782,"title":"","content":"I think the second dot giving complete immunity to a discipline is very overpowered, as is being able to reflexively 'veto' other ones at that level. Really, that's potent even for five if it doesn't have even a clash of wills roll.<br /> <br /> That said, I really like the idea of this Coil, it's very cool thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:16:30-07:00","id":450874,"title":"","content":"It doesn't entirely supply immunity, and only supplies that immunity against <i>direct</i> uses by the guy affected. So you would be immune to, say, Auspex directly asking questions about you, or Dominate,but it wouldn't protect you from them using it on other people.<br /> <br /> The veto, however, is a bit undercosted - again, I think I'm going to revise this one when I get the inspiration (&quot;today&quot; might have been too optimistic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:31:09-07:00","id":450897,"title":"","content":"It's still overpowered. For the cost of a merit, you can make yourself immune to an entire discipline line simply by purchasing the first rank of a discipline because Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare etc. require the first rank of that power in order to use subsequent ranks. And that's pretty shitty of an ST to allow someone to effortlessly and cost free completely invalidate someone else's ability when they invested in multiple ranks in a power, with no resistance or means to reverse it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 03-20-2015, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:51:35-07:00","id":450909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/449777-mystery-the-mystery-of-vitalic-philosophy?p=450897#post450897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still overpowered. For the cost of a merit, you can make yourself immune to an entire discipline line simply by purchasing the first rank of a discipline because Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare etc. require the first rank of that power in order to use subsequent ranks. And that's pretty shitty of an ST to allow someone to effortlessly and cost free completely invalidate someone else's ability when they invested in multiple ranks in a power, with no resistance or means to reverse it.</div> </div> </div> </div> While you have a valid point, I'm confused by what you mean by &quot;For the cost of a Merit&quot;. Since this is a Coil, the cost to get the two Coil dots and the one Discipline dot vary from 12 xp(if both unfavored) to 9 xp(if both favored), 7 xp if the Ordo merit Crucible(from the Secrets of the Covenants preview) is used. If you mean sacrificing one of your starting Disciplines in order to start out with this and then buying the second dot, you would reduce it down to 3 xp if you've favored it(2 if using Crucible), which comes close to your point, except that all this is assuming you only want to use this against a single Discipline. To summarize, while I agree that this should probably be looked into, it takes a lot of xp according to the current system. And of course, this assumes a PC is using it instead of a npc. Sorry if I'm being a bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:57:41-07:00","id":450913,"title":"","content":"From one person.<br /> <br /> Who had to be fed your blood.<br /> <br /> Directly from your body.<br /> <br /> Who then counts against your total uses of the Coil.<br /> <br /> And you have to renew this protection each night.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Invictus can render themselves immune to another Invictus' Discipline use <i>permanently</i> for a few XP.<br /> <br /> For reference, a Mortal can buy a <i>two dot</i> merit that renders them immune to Nightmare, Obfuscate, and any other Discipline that creates an illusion for a scene. It costs them one Willpower to keep it up.<br /> <br /> Immunity to Discipline effects that <i>directly target you</i> is not as overpowered as you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:05:19-07:00","id":450921,"title":"","content":"An Oath needs to be sworn between two people, it's not something they can just apply to anyone, so that's not really a proper comparison.<br /> <br /> And the clear sighted merit only works for a scene, by spending willpower. And that's only on illusion; not exactly the most overpowered sort of thing to be immune to. Plus, it's vanilla mortal only, and a lot of mortal only merits are much cheaper than the equivalent for another splat.<br /> <br /> Notice that the closest equivalent for any sort of mind control (a lot of other disciplines) gives you nothing but a few bonus dice. You have to consider what you can become immune to when balancing something, and how exactly it works, not just that it's immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T22:02:15-07:00","id":477526,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's a revision of it (which I think works out better.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Mystery of Vitalic Philosophy (Revised)</span><br /> Through a regimen of meditations and self-imposed surgeries, a Dragon twists the flow of Vitae through their dead veins, bringing it to new heights of vicious pleasure and terrible strength. By undergoing this transformation, they fully assert the nature of their Clan, becoming gore-drenched and iconic.<br /> Let the Crones keep their blood-sorcery, and the Invictus their Oaths - the Ordo Dracul has its Blood-Saints.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Coil of Vitalic Philosophy</span><br /> <b>Perfecting Crass Gore (\u2022):</b> Blood is strength, as is the Vitae intermingled with it; the ascending bloody Bodhisattva knows this more fully than perhaps anyone else. The Dragon selects one of their in-Clan Disciplines to Enlighten; while a Discipline is Enlightened, its dot rating is increased by one for all purposes other than qualifying for Devotions. If this would improve the Discipline's rating past 5, they do not gain any additional, transcendental powers; it merely shows that they've reached perfection within it.<br /> They may even Empower a Discipline they do not actually have dots in, unlocking the secrets inherent in their curse. They may change which Discipline they have Enlightened by spending an hour meditating and spending one Vitae, old knowledge bloodily subsumed beneath the new; they may only have one Discipline Enlightened by this Coil at any one time, and all Enlightened Disciplines must be in-Clan for the them.<br /> <br /> <b>Hearing the Clumsy Flow (\u2022\u2022):</b> To those chasing perfection, the clumsy powers of the uninitiated are laughably obvious. The Dragon can hear the use of any Discipline they currently have Enlightened; each Dragon describes the exact sound differently, but it shares the same sharp urgency as the heart-beats of the living. Similarly, if the Enlightened Discipline has a lasting effect, the Dragon can see it as if it was a bloodstain; a Ventrue Dragon could see the bloody marks of Dominate in the eyes of the victims, while a Daeva might see the bloody war-paint of Vigor. This step of the Coil is not sufficient to pierce the benefits of Obfuscate or similar effects; however, it is enough to initiate a Clash of Wills to do so, using Resolve + Composure + Blood Potency as their dice-pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightenment in the Blood (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> The Dragon no longer sees any difference between their own will and the will of the Beast when they bring to bear their chosen power. They may now have two Enlightened Disciplines at any given time; they may only exchange one through each act of meditation. In addition, they may spend Willpower and Vitae interchangeably when using any of their Enlightened Disciplines; this includes spending &quot;Willpower&quot; to improve an activation dice-pool, though they can only spend one &quot;Willpower&quot; to improve a given roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Wearing Scarlet Robes (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> It is folly to believe that the toys of lesser Kindred are anything like the raw, vibrant potency of a Blood-Sage's chosen tools; a bloody halo marks their inviolate nature for all to see. The Dragon may wrap their nature around them like a cloak, becoming temporarily transcendent. As long as they adopt this mantle, they are obviously inhuman, wreathed in hallucinations hinting at their refined nature; as such, they cannot activate the Blush of Life while doing so, and they suffer from an additional Bane for the duration, chosen upon learning this rank of the Coil.<br /> While in this state, they apply their dots in this Coil as a penalty to any dice-pool rolled against them that involves one of their Enlightened Disciplines; this includes activation rolls, as well as any roll that receives a bonus due to the Discipline, whether directly or due to it increasing an Attribute or trait. This &quot;cloak&quot; lasts for one scene unless the Dragon enters Torpor, in which case it lasts until they awaken.<br /> <br /> <b>A Corpse-Shrine of Vitae (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> This level of enlightenment is rarely reached; most Dragons that pursue this Mystery balk at the particular restrictions this state brings. But still, it has been reached before, and the results are <i>legendary</i>. Upon reaching this level of the Coil, all of the Dragon's in-Clan Disciplines become Enlightened, and their transcendental state becomes permanent. However, the drain of this perfected state forces them to spend one Vitae each scene they spend awake outside of a Dragon's Nest; failure to do so causes them to slip into Torpor.<br /> <hr /><br /> Ideas for Scales include stuff like using certain Yantras with your Disciplines, awakening bloody powers similar to your Clan's within other characters, a Down-and-Dirty Spellcasting (see Mage 2e when it comes out) for their Disciplines, and other fun stuff. It's all screaming &quot;fuck you&quot; at the Divine by becoming Divine yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T02:27:10-07:00","id":477690,"title":"","content":"While the coil looks fine to me, the fluff around it seems over the top to me. <br /> <br /> Except the 5th dot, I don't like seeing that limitation there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}